# Line endings are LF in the repository and LF in every checkout, Windows included.
#
# Without this, git converts on checkout for Windows contributors, and every lock that
# reads a committed file and compares it to something generated fails there and nowhere
# else. That has happened four times in this repository — the flagstaff R4 source lock, the
# gallery staleness lock, and twice more — each time fixed by normalising inside the test,
# which treats the symptom in one place and leaves the next lock to rediscover it.
#
# `eol=lf` is the fix at the cause. The workarounds already written stay: they cost a
# `replaceAll` and they keep those tests honest for anyone whose git predates this file or
# who checked out before it landed.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary, never converted and never diffed as text.
*.png binary
*.gif binary
*.svg text eol=lf
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary

# Vendored suites are the hosts' own bytes. A conversion here would change what we grade,
# and the compatibility record fingerprints these files.
packages/compat-oracle/vendor/** -text
